  "intro": "<p>Love names fall into two groups: names that mean love itself, like Carys (Welsh), Aroha (Māori) or Sevgi (Turkish), and names that mean beloved or dear, which is a much older idea. Amy, Mabel, David, Kevin and Priya are all in the second group, and several of them are among the most-used names in England and Wales. Every meaning here has been checked against a cited source, mostly Behind the Name and Wiktionary, and the ranks come from the ONS.</p><p>Love is also where baby name myths cluster. Romeo, Valentine and Freya are linked with love by story and tradition, not by meaning. We've marked them uncertain and explained.</p>",
