  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Beloved names",
      "content": "<p>Names meaning 'beloved' or 'dear' are some of the oldest in use. David comes from Hebrew <em>dod</em>, Amy from Old French <em>amée</em>, Kevin from Irish <em>cóem</em>, Priya from Sanskrit and Habib from Arabic. If you want a love meaning in a name people already know, start here.</p>"
    },
    {
      "heading": "The Sikh -preet names",
      "content": "<p>Many Sikh names end in <em>-preet</em>, from Sanskrit <em>prīti</em>, 'love'. They're used for both boys and girls: Harpreet is 'love of Hari (God)', Gurpreet 'love of the guru', Manpreet 'love of the mind'. The first part changes the sense, so it's worth knowing what each one means before you choose.</p>"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Nicknames and short forms",
      "content": "<p>Amabel gives Mabel or Bel, Philomena gives Mina, Jedidiah gives Jed, and Amadeus gives Amadeo or Deo. David has Dave, Davy and Dai in Welsh. If you're choosing a long love name, try the short form too, because that's what most people will use.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "faqs": [
    {
      "question": "What name means loved by God?",
      "answer": "Jedidiah means 'beloved of Yahweh' in Hebrew, and Amadeus 'love of God' in Latin. Olufemi, from Yoruba, means 'God loves me'."
    },
    {
      "question": "What name means lover of horses?",
      "answer": "Philip, from Greek Philippos, made of philos ('friend, lover') and hippos ('horse'). Philippa is the feminine form."
    },
    {
      "question": "What girl names mean love?",
      "answer": "Carys (Welsh), Ahava (Hebrew), Kerensa (Cornish), Lyubov (Russian), Sevgi (Turkish) and Aiko (Japanese) mean love. Amy, Mabel, Davina, Caoimhe and Priya mean beloved or dear."
    }
  ],
